# Neustack E-Commerce Application

`docker compose up --build` to start database, application and pgadmin containers, data will be seeded using init.sql

`docker compose down -v` to stop the containers.

`python3 test_api.py` runs API tests when the containers are up. This must be run before any APIs are called else it may fail because of changes in database.

`spring-boot-collection.postman_collection.json` - import into postman to use the API's when the containers are running.

pgAdmin is available at `http://localhost:5050`. Login is bypassed (`PGADMIN_CONFIG_SERVER_MODE: "False"`), and the database server connection is automatically pre-configured and authenticated via `servers.json` and `pgpass`.
It takes a while for pgAdmin to startup.
